From: ios-blink-sideload <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:39:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS sideload: page insets after a half turn

Turning the phone from one landscape side to the other moves Chrome's
App Bar across the screen, but the view keeps its size, so
-viewWillTransitionToSize: isn't called, and that is where
BrowserViewController invalidates the page's insets. The page kept the
inset of the side the App Bar had left and lay partly under the App Bar
on the other side, with a gray strip where the inset still was (seen on
an iPhone 13 mini). Invalidate the inset range when the App Bar changes
position too.

Status: verified at Chromium 3313f827 in the iOS 27 simulator: after
turning left and then straight to the right (and back), the scroll
view's insets follow the App Bar and the page lies right next to it,
whole; before, the insets kept the old side ({62, 0, 0, 68} with the bar
on the left) and the page was 68 points under the bar. Not checked on a
device.

diff --git a/ios/chrome/browser/browser_view/ui_bundled/browser_view_controller.mm b/ios/chrome/browser/browser_view/ui_bundled/browser_view_controller.mm
index 24201af6ec2324603dd1d78856c03da8dc4ce241..2317acc5deabd38a3b130f877f324327c4a66527 100644
--- a/ios/chrome/browser/browser_view/ui_bundled/browser_view_controller.mm
+++ b/ios/chrome/browser/browser_view/ui_bundled/browser_view_controller.mm
@@ -703,6 +703,14 @@ - (void)layoutState:(SceneLayoutState*)layoutState
   [self updateToolbarConstraints];
   [self updateSecondaryToolbarBottomConstraint];
   [self animateTransition];
+  // [ios-blink-sideload] The page's insets follow the App Bar too. Turning the
+  // phone from one landscape side to the other moves the App Bar across but
+  // keeps the view's size, so -viewWillTransitionToSize: isn't called to
+  // invalidate them: the page stayed inset on the side the App Bar left, and
+  // partly under the App Bar on the other side.
+  if (IsFullscreenRefactoringEnabled() && _fullscreenBrowserAgent) {
+    _fullscreenBrowserAgent->InvalidateInsetRange();
+  }
 }
 
 #pragma mark - Public methods
